Article 82 Where any of the following acts is committed in violation of the provisions of this Law, the competent environmental protection department of the people's government at or above the county level shall order correction within a time limit and impose a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; if correction is not made within the time limit, the violator shall be ordered to suspend production for remediation:
(1) Failing to self-monitor the discharged water pollutants in accordance with regulations, or failing to keep original monitoring records;
(2) Failing to install automatic monitoring equipment for water pollutant discharge in accordance with regulations, failing to connect with the monitoring equipment of the competent environmental protection department in accordance with regulations, or failing to ensure the normal operation of the monitoring equipment;
(3) Failing to monitor the sewage outlets and surrounding environment for toxic and hazardous water pollutants in accordance with regulations, or failing to disclose information on toxic and hazardous water pollutants.

Article 83 Where any of the following acts is committed in violation of the provisions of this Law, the competent environmental protection department of the people's government at or above the county level shall order correction or restrict production or suspend production for remediation, and concurrently impose a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, the matter shall be submitted to the people's government with the authority to approve for approval to order business suspension or closure:
(1) Discharging water pollutants without lawfully obtaining a pollutant discharge permit;
(2) Discharging water pollutants in excess of the water pollutant discharge standards or in excess of the total amount control indicators for the discharge of key water pollutants;
(3) Discharging water pollutants by means of escape from supervision, such as using seepage wells, seepage pits, crevices, karst caves, secretly setting up pipes, falsifying or forging monitoring data, or operating water pollution prevention and control facilities abnormally;
(4) Failing to conduct pretreatment in accordance with regulations and discharging industrial wastewater that does not meet the treatment process requirements into centralized sewage treatment facilities.

Article 85 Where any of the following acts is committed, the competent environmental protection department of the local people's government at or above the county level shall order the cessation of the illegal act, require remedial measures within a time limit to eliminate pollution, and impose a fine; if remedial measures are not taken within the time limit, the competent environmental protection department may designate a unit with the capacity to carry out the remedial measures on behalf of the violator, with the expenses borne by the violator:
(1) Discharging oil, acid liquids, or alkaline liquids into water bodies;
(2) Discharging highly toxic waste liquids into water bodies, or discharging, dumping, or directly burying soluble highly toxic waste residues containing mercury, cadmium, arsenic, chromium, lead, cyanides, yellow phosphorus, etc. into water bodies or underground;
(3) Washing vehicles or containers that have stored oil or toxic pollutants in water bodies;
(4) Discharging or dumping industrial waste residues, urban garbage, or other wastes into water bodies, or piling, storing solid wastes or other pollutants on beaches or banks below the highest water level of rivers, lakes, canals, channels, or reservoirs;
(5) Discharging or dumping radioactive solid wastes or wastewater containing high or intermediate radioactive substances into water bodies;
(6) Discharging wastewater containing low radioactive substances, thermal wastewater, or sewage containing pathogens into water bodies in violation of relevant State provisions or standards;
(7) Failing to take anti-leakage measures, or failing to construct groundwater quality monitoring wells for monitoring;
(8) Underground oil tanks of gas stations, etc. failing to use double-layer tanks or take other effective measures such as building anti-leakage pools, or failing to conduct anti-leakage monitoring;
(9) Failing to take protective measures in accordance with regulations, or using ditches, pits, or ponds without anti-leakage measures to transport or store wastewater containing toxic pollutants, sewage containing pathogens, or other wastes.
For any of the acts specified in items (3), (4), (6), (7), or (8) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed. For any of the acts specified in items (1), (2), (5), or (9) of the preceding paragraph, a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 1,000,000 yuan shall be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, the matter shall be submitted to the people's government with the authority to approve for approval to order business suspension or closure.

Article 90 Where any of the following acts is committed in violation of the provisions of this Law, the maritime administrative agency or the competent fishery department shall, within their respective functions and duties, order the cessation of the illegal act and impose a fine of not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan; if water pollution is caused, the violator shall be ordered to take remedial measures within a time limit to eliminate pollution, and a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan shall be imposed; if remedial measures are not taken within the time limit, the maritime administrative agency or the competent fishery department may, within their respective functions and duties, designate a unit with the capacity to carry out the remedial measures on behalf of the violator, with the expenses borne by the ship:
(1) Dumping ship garbage into water bodies or discharging residual oil or waste oil from ships;
(2) A ship carrying out lightering operations of bulk liquid pollution-hazardous cargo without the approval of the maritime administrative agency at the place of operation;
(3) Ships and relevant operating units engaging in operational activities with pollution risks without taking pollution prevention measures in accordance with regulations;
(4) Dismantling ships by beaching;
(5) International voyage ships entering the inland rivers of the People's Republic of China discharging ship ballast water that does not comply with regulations.

Article 91 Where any of the following acts is committed, the competent environmental protection department of the local people's government at or above the county level shall order the cessation of the illegal act, impose a fine of not less than 100,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan, and submit the matter to the people's government with the authority to approve for approval to order demolition or closure:
(1) Constructing, renovating, or expanding construction projects unrelated to water supply facilities and water source protection in first-grade drinking water source protection zones;
(2) Constructing, renovating, or expanding construction projects that discharge pollutants in second-grade drinking water source protection zones;
(3) Constructing or expanding construction projects that cause serious water pollution, or renovating construction projects that increase the amount of pollutant discharge in quasi-protection zones of drinking water sources.
Where cage culture is engaged in, or tourism, angling, or other activities that may pollute drinking water bodies are organized in first-grade drinking water source protection zones, the competent environmental protection department of the local people's government at or above the county level shall order the cessation of the illegal act and impose a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan. Where an individual swims, angles, or engages in other activities that may pollute drinking water bodies in first-grade drinking water source protection zones, the competent environmental protection department of the local people's government at or above the county level shall order the cessation of the illegal act and may impose a fine of not more than 500 yuan.

Article 93 Where an enterprise or public institution commits any of the following acts, the competent environmental protection department of the people's government at or above the county level shall order correction; if the circumstances are serious, a fine of not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan shall be imposed:
(1) Failing to formulate an emergency plan for water pollution accidents in accordance with regulations;
(2) Failing to promptly activate the emergency plan for water pollution accidents and take relevant emergency measures after a water pollution accident occurs.
